# Forms, Queries and Reports Build Guide

## Main navigation
- `frmLogin`: username/password inputs; validate user, set TempVars `UserID`, `UserRole`, `ActiveShopID`.
- `frmDashboard`: KPI cards and buttons to open modules.
- `frmShopList`: Record Source `tblShops`.
- `frmProductList`: Record Source `tblProducts`; filter/search by SKU, barcode, name, category.
- `frmCustomerList`: Record Source `tblCustomers`.
- `frmSupplierList`: Record Source `tblSuppliers`.
- `frmPOS`: unbound product search/barcode box, quantity, cart subform `sfrmPOSLines`, customer selector, totals, payment method, Post Sale button.
- `frmPurchase`: purchase header with purchase lines subform; Post Purchase button.
- `frmStock`: shop selector and stock query.
- `frmStockTransfer`: source shop, destination shop, transfer lines; Dispatch and Receive actions.
- `frmIMEIRegister`: IMEI, product, shop, purchase reference, status and warranty dates.
- `frmExpenses`: Record Source `tblExpenses`.
- `frmUserAdmin`: Record Source `tblUsers`; admin only.
- `frmReports`: report launcher.

## Required saved queries
Create queries using SQL View. Refer to `Database/QUERY_CATALOG.md`.

## Reports
- `rptSalesInvoice`: grouped by SaleID; show invoice number, shop, date, customer, line items, subtotal, discount, tax, grand total, paid and balance.
- `rptDailySales`: group by date and shop; sum gross, discount, tax and net sales.
- `rptProductStock`: shop, SKU, product, quantity, reorder level, stock value.
- `rptLowStock`: products where QtyOnHand <= ReorderLevel.
- `rptIMEIWarranty`: IMEI, product, customer, sale date, warranty end.
- `rptCustomerLedger`: opening balance plus sales and receipts.
- `rptSupplierLedger`: purchases and payments.
- `rptProfitSummary`: sales less cost of goods sold; exclude expenses unless separately shown.
- `rptExpenseSummary`: expenses by category, shop and date range.
- `rptStockTransfer`: transfer document with dispatch/receive status.

## Dashboard KPIs
Use DSum / DCount only for small datasets; for larger datasets use aggregate saved queries:
- Today's net sales
- Month-to-date sales
- Current stock value
- Low-stock item count
- Customer receivables
- Supplier payables
- Today's expenses

## Form event pattern
Set a command button's On Click to `[Event Procedure]`, then use:
`Private Sub cmdOpenProducts_Click(): DoCmd.OpenForm "frmProductList": End Sub`
